 "note": "The analytic limit is rescaled to the measured visit count before the ratio is taken, because the limit falls as 1/sqrt(visits) and the archive lists more visits than were acquired. What remains is the difference between a 5 sigma Gaussian cut on the archive variance and the empirical p95 of the null on the measured scatter. The measured value is the one to quote; the analytic value is a cross-check, not a second measurement. The two also sit at different false-positive rates: the analytic cut at 5 sigma admits about 3e-7 of the noise, the measured cut at the p95 admits 5 percent. A looser cut reaches fainter flux, so the measured limit is lower by construction, and the ratio is the price of the looser cut rather than a disagreement between two estimates of one number."
